Freedoom's DEHACKED lump, and an exit function WebAssembly can call.

DEH_String becomes a function (the add-on's src/deh_lite.c) where doomgeneric left Chocolate Doom's
dehacked code out (FEATURE_DEHACKED off): an IWAD's own DEHACKED lump is read where Chocolate Doom
loads it (LoadIwadDeh, under ORIGCODE here) — Freedoom's: its texts (BEX [STRINGS]: level names,
messages, the stories between episodes), changed frames and par times. Freedoom needs it ("The
Freedoom IWADs have DEHACKED lumps that must be loaded"); without it the game shows the original
game's texts. -nodeh leaves it out, as in Chocolate Doom.

G_CheckDemoStatus returns a boolean and was registered as an exit function (void (*)(void)) by a
cast: WebAssembly calls a function only as what it is, and the call at exit trapped (the program
ended with SIGSEGV instead of 0 after -timedemo, -shot, quitting). A void wrapper is registered.

diff --git a/doomgeneric/d_main.c b/doomgeneric/d_main.c
index 9012e5f..c9518cd 100644
--- a/doomgeneric/d_main.c
+++ b/doomgeneric/d_main.c
@@ -1157,6 +1157,13 @@ static void LoadIwadDeh(void)
 }
 #endif
 
+// doomterm: an exit function returns nothing; G_CheckDemoStatus returns a boolean, and
+// WebAssembly calls a function only as what it is (a cast pointer to it traps)
+static void CheckDemoStatusAtExit(void)
+{
+    G_CheckDemoStatus();
+}
+
 //
 // D_DoomMain
 //
@@ -1401,6 +1408,12 @@ void D_DoomMain (void)
         // them to be played properly.
         LoadIwadDeh();
     }
+#else
+    if (!M_ParmExists("-nodeh"))
+    {
+        // doomterm: Freedoom's DEHACKED lump (its texts, frames, par times)
+        DEH_LoadIwadLump();
+    }
 #endif
 
     // Doom 3: BFG Edition includes modified versions of the classic
@@ -1510,7 +1523,7 @@ void D_DoomMain (void)
         printf("Playing demo %s.\n", file);
     }
 
-    I_AtExit((atexit_func_t) G_CheckDemoStatus, true);
+    I_AtExit(CheckDemoStatusAtExit, true);
 
     // Generate the WAD hash table.  Speed things up a bit.
     W_GenerateHashTable();
diff --git a/doomgeneric/deh_str.h b/doomgeneric/deh_str.h
index cdecaf0..88830a0 100644
--- a/doomgeneric/deh_str.h
+++ b/doomgeneric/deh_str.h
@@ -35,7 +35,9 @@ void DEH_AddStringReplacement(char *from_text, char *to_text);
 
 #else
 
-#define DEH_String(x) (x)
+// doomterm: the texts of an IWAD's DEHACKED lump ([STRINGS]; deh_lite.c)
+char *DEH_String(char *s);
+void DEH_LoadIwadLump(void);
 #define DEH_printf printf
 #define DEH_fprintf fprintf
 #define DEH_snprintf snprintf
